[{"id":92258,"sender_id":753,"sender_full_name":"mattecapu","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/187d4d9e4d0204d30511b008839315ab?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/92258\">#1</a> I noticed I split my edits between this username and the anonymous name 'Matteo Capucci'.<br>Is there an _easy_ way to move the anonymous ones to my main account?</p>","timestamp":1625412424,"subject":"Change edits author","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":92310,"sender_id":237,"sender_full_name":"Richard Williamson","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b90dbe6063b47a44f7308efebb6ade2b?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/92310\">#2</a> Hi Matteo, I have done this now. I am not sure why the anonymous ones are not being automatically associated to your account, they should be I think as you have provided your name in your nForum account details (unless you only added this info very recently). Let me know if this continues and I will investigate!</p>","timestamp":1625557295,"subject":"Change edits author","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":92321,"sender_id":753,"sender_full_name":"mattecapu","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/187d4d9e4d0204d30511b008839315ab?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/92321\">#3</a> Yes I added the ‘real name’ in order to try to merge the two edit groups.\nThanks a lot!</p>","timestamp":1625567548,"subject":"Change edits author","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":92322,"sender_id":753,"sender_full_name":"mattecapu","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/187d4d9e4d0204d30511b008839315ab?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/92322\">#4</a> I still see all my 2021 edits under <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/author/Matteo%20Capucci\">‘Matteo Capucci’</a> instead of <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/author/mattecapu\">‘mattecapu’</a></p>","timestamp":1625567647,"subject":"Change edits author","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":92331,"sender_id":237,"sender_full_name":"Richard Williamson","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b90dbe6063b47a44f7308efebb6ade2b?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/92331\">#5</a> Re <a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/92321\">#3</a>: that explains it, thanks!</p>\n<p>Re <a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/92322\">#4</a>: yes, the way it works now is that when you sign an nLab edit as ‘Matteo Capucci’, it will be associated with your nforum account ‘mattecapu’ correctly. I didn’t realise that you had made nLab edits in both names, I only fixed things on the nForum. I can change nLab edits signed as ‘mattecapu’ to ‘Matteo Capucci’, is that OK/what you wish?</p>","timestamp":1625573253,"subject":"Change edits author","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":92336,"sender_id":753,"sender_full_name":"mattecapu","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/187d4d9e4d0204d30511b008839315ab?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/92336\">#6</a> Yes, if that means I can sign with my real name and sitll be associated with this nForum account.\nThanks again for the help :)</p>","timestamp":1625576173,"subject":"Change edits author","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":92374,"sender_id":237,"sender_full_name":"Richard Williamson","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b90dbe6063b47a44f7308efebb6ade2b?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/92374\">#7</a> Yes, that is how it should work from now on. I have changed the name of your nLab edits now to all be ‘Matteo Capucci’.</p>","timestamp":1625660947,"subject":"Change edits author","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":92393,"sender_id":753,"sender_full_name":"mattecapu","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/187d4d9e4d0204d30511b008839315ab?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/92393\">#8</a> Amazing, thanks!</p>","timestamp":1625737232,"subject":"Change edits author","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":105445,"sender_id":853,"sender_full_name":"BryceClarke","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/542e818f22daa3230848830f8ba54e03?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/105445\">#9</a> So I have just noticed that my edits have also been splitting: see here <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/author/Bryce+Clarke\">https://ncatlab.org/nlab/author/Bryce+Clarke</a> and here <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/author/BryceClarke\">https://ncatlab.org/nlab/author/BryceClarke</a>. Is it possible for these to be merged?</p>","timestamp":1676538990,"subject":"Change edits author","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":105448,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/105448\">#10</a> I don’t know, but I’ll check with the technical team.</p>","timestamp":1676542676,"subject":"Change edits author","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":105464,"sender_id":1023,"sender_full_name":"Christian Sattler","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/757f09611d69fda7988c64298ff925e9?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/105464\">#11</a> The nLab edits have been unified under author \"Bryce Clarke\".</p>\n<p>Cached pages may still show the old author name until the cache is cleared (for example on page edit).</p>","timestamp":1676588147,"subject":"Change edits author","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":105474,"sender_id":853,"sender_full_name":"BryceClarke","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/542e818f22daa3230848830f8ba54e03?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Change.20edits.20author/near/105474\">#12</a> Thank you very much!</p>","timestamp":1676623564,"subject":"Change edits author","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]}]